Sure.  You know what icon tooltypes are, right?  If you don't, check your
AmigaDos reference manual.  But since you probably don't want to go dig out
the docs (who does?), the short form is, every icon has information stored in
it in the form of tooltypes.  When you launch NetHack from HackWB, it uses
the tooltypes of the NewGame icon to set preferences.  These preferences can
override preferences in your NetHack.cnf file.

So... where's the info command?  It's in the HackWB program, NOT the NetHack
program.  Within HackWB, you should find "Info" as a pulldown menu item or
some such.  Fiddle with it enough, you'll figure out how to edit icon
tooltypes.

Of course, I don't like to use HackWB for editing my preferences and tooltypes
because (a) I use fonts other than Topaz 8, and it seems that HackWB will
use your System font preferences but will not adjust things accordingly.
Hence, gadgets will get screwed up if you use a big enough font; (b) HackWB
has a nasty habit of altering tooltypes I *don't* want it to alter when I go
into it to fix something; (c) HackWB isn't intelligent enough to handle the
character limit of Amiga icon tooltypes.  So when using that nifty
preferences editor in HackWB, if you pick certain options (and enough of them)
and if you give reasonably long names to your dog, cat, and favorite fruit,
well gosh, it'll clip the tooltype line short.

How to avoid problems with HackWB?

In Workbench, go into the NetHack directory where the NewGame icon is stored.
Edit it with the workbench "Information..." pulldown menu option.  You can
edit the tooltypes easily this way.

